get.description:
Post-clean monitoring from the issue lifecycle: per ISO week the records that failed again (``reopened``) and
the records fixed (``auto_resolved``); per rule the same counts plus the last four weeks against the four before;
per fix batch the records it fixed and how many of those came back after it was created.

post.description:
Aletheia's wording of the break. The model gets the break's kind, the rule or field code and its text, and the
aggregate figures: never a record or a value. Its sentences are kept only when every number is one of the figures;
otherwise (or with no model) the deterministic explanation is stored and shown.

get.description:
Why this is a break: the robust z against the values of the baseline runs, the DDIC definition of the field and,
for a cardinality or shape shift, the codes that came and went, checked against the live check table. Deterministic;
nothing is sent to a model.

post.description:
Sign out: clear the session cookie and write an ``auth.logout`` audit row.

Behind LocalAuthMiddleware, so only a signed-in caller reaches it. The browser drops its own token;
other sessions of the same user stay valid (changing the password is what revokes them).
